    "created_at": "2026-10-01T18:24:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T18:24:00Z",
    "body": "Web Serial now provides a useful Chromium implementation precedent for this experiment.\n\n`SerialPortUnderlyingSource::ReadDataOrArmWatcher()` checks `ReadableStreamBYOBRequest`, limits the Mojo read span to the caller-provided view, copies into that view, and calls `respond()` instead of allocating/enqueuing a fresh JS chunk.\n\nWebUSB still returns a newly-created `USBInTransferResult` from `transferIn()`.\n\nIt may be worth benchmarking the same high-rate device workload through:\n1. current WebUSB,\n2. a prototype caller-owned buffer,\n3. Web Serial's BYOB path as a reference.\n\nThat should separate JS allocation/GC savings from USB/Mojo transport cost.\n",
